{2}{5}=\\frac{6}{1}\\times \\frac{5}{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. Note that we can simplify the process by swapping the denominators first.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6}{1}\\times \\frac{5}{2} & =\\frac{6}{2}\\times \\frac{5}{1} \\\\  & =3\\times 5 \\\\  & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432148 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186142805 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8e58a7d0-dfe1-52dd-9de0-f598aca658df" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing Whole Numbers by Unit Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30e92b0a-a529-58dc-ba44-0446b7ea469f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432070} {:answer/id #uuid "30ed298a-f7cb-50cc-9038-3ff710a67bda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432071} {:answer/id #uuid "3fc51103-9cb2-5bd0-ba07-c2aede4ec7cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432077} {:answer/id #uuid "9f0f8ea8-e870-5aab-8b86-df17b61d6a84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432095} {:answer/id #uuid "ec23de19-b7fb-56b5-9312-e202747aa452" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f0f8ea8-e870-5aab-8b86-df17b61d6a84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432095} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b870f3b-afe0-542d-8844-b02e37033176" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432129}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.d