3-f0d2-53cf-b184-a6872080a447" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432122}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c0abb3e-b307-5eda-92d0-4b63963ecd86" :question/math-academy-id "q-99937" :question/problem "$8÷\\frac{3}{7}=$" :question/worked-solution "Dividing a whole number by a fraction is equivalent to multiplying the whole number by the reciprocal of the fraction.\n\nFirst, we write $8$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n8=\\frac{8}{1}\n$$\n\nNext, we note that the reciprocal of $\\frac{3}{7}$ is $\\frac{7}{3}.$ \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n8÷\\frac{3}{7}=\\frac{8}{1}÷\\frac{3}{7}=\\frac{8}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply our fractions. \n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{1}\\times \\frac{7}{3}=\\frac{8\\times 7}{1\\times 3}=\\frac{56}{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the resulting improper fraction as a mixed number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{56}{3}=18\\,\\text{R}\\,2=18\\,\\frac{2}{3}\n$$"}]}
